              <div class="Section1"> 
                <p class="MsoNormal"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><o:p>PMWATCH 
                  - Feb. 20, 2002 -- As public opinion is quickly shifting against 
                  him, as <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/reservegenerals.asp">IDF soldiers begin to 
                  refuse serving in the OT</a>, and as the Palestinians at long 
                  last are seriously building a </o:p></font><o:p><a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/nonviolence.asp"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">non-violent 
                  resistence movement</font></a></o:p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><o:p>, 
                  <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/sharon.asp">Ariel Sharon</a> is scrambling for his 
                  dear political life and frantically trying to escalate the violence 
                  and tip the conflict into full warfare. Today, 16 Palestinians 
                  were brutally killed in one of the bloodiest assaults against 
                  the Palestinians since the Intifada started 17 months ago.</o:p></font></p>
                <p class="MsoNormal"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><o:p>And 
                  yet, obvious as <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/autopsy.asp">Sharon's 
                  desperation moves</a> may appear to anyone watching on the sidelines, 
                  the US media continues to resist taking a strong stand against 
                  Sharon and to call on the US administration to stand up and 
                  tell Sharon that ENOUGH IS ENOUGH!</o:p></font></p>
                <p class="MsoNormal"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Below 
                  is an interface that will shoot off your letter to all the main 
                  US newspapers.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Please 
                  make sure your voice is heard and tell them ENOUGH! The media 
                  needs to take a strong stand and to support the emerging alternative 
                  rather than allow Sharon to keep the bloodletting going. </font></p>
                <p class="MsoNormal"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Sharon 
                  is done and he needs to go. He has handsomely served to illustrate 
                  the total bankruptcy of his "iron policy against terrorism" 
                  and so his time is up!<span style="mso-spacerun: yes"> Not that 
                  his role in making history is over. Next stop: <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/sharon.asp">Brussels</a>!</span></font></p>
                <p class="MsoNormal"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Please 
                  mobilize and ask your friends to join in a campaign to shake 
                  the media out of its comfortable trance. </font><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Fill</font><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                  your personal information, add your comments, and then click 
                  send. </font></p>
